## Versioning & Upgrade Rules

1. **Do not** silently bump major versions of: `next`, `react`, `react-dom`, `tailwindcss`, `@reduxjs/toolkit`, `zod`, `react-hook-form`, `@sentry/nextjs`, `@logtail/next`, `react-leaflet`, `pdfjs-dist`. These have peer-dependency or breaking-API impact across the app.
2. When adding a dependency, **check peer ranges against `next@16` and `react@19`**. Reject anything that pins `next <15` or `react <18`.
3. Prefer existing libraries listed above over functionally equivalent newcomers (e.g., do not add `moment`, `formik`, `yup`, `zustand`, `swr`, `tanstack-query`, `styled-components`, `emotion`).
4. After any dependency change, run `npm install` (no `--legacy-peer-deps` unless explicitly approved) and update this rule if you add/remove a major lib.

## Quick "do/don't" cheatsheet

```ts
// ✅ async params (Next 16)
export default async function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {
  const { id } = await params;
}

// ✅ class merging
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
<div className={cn("p-4", isActive && "bg-primary-50")} />

// ✅ form
const form = useForm<Values>({ resolver: zodResolver(schema) });

// ❌ don't add forwardRef in new components (React 19)
const Btn = React.forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, Props>((p, ref) => <button ref={ref} {...p} />);

// ❌ don't call axios directly in a component
const data = await axios.get("/api/orders"); // use src/api RTK Query module

// ❌ don't introduce new toast lib
import { toast } from "react-hot-toast"; // use sonner
```
